# Line-ending and binary-safety rules for c-rust-learning.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Every quality gate runs through a bash script under
# code/src/scripts/ and every hook under .claude/hooks/ is bash. A checkout that
# rewrites line endings to CRLF (core.autocrlf=true on a Windows clone) breaks them
# with errors that name neither the file nor the cause. Measured 27/09/2026 on
# bash 5.2 with a CRLF copy of a two-line script:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#     set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# Kernel patches carry the same risk later: scripts/checkpatch.pl rejects DOS line
# endings, so a P5 patch series normalised to CRLF would fail the kernel's own check.
#
# Normalising here removes the whole class on every clone, without asking anyone to
# configure git correctly first.

# ── Text ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree. Nothing
# here wants CRLF: there is no .bat, .cmd or .ps1 in the tree, and every tool that
# reads these files (bash, gcc, make, cargo, the kernel build) is POSIX.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stated again for the files where a CRLF is a failure rather than a cosmetic
# difference — a shebang, a make recipe, a toolchain pin, a patch. Redundant against
# the rule above by design: these are the lines someone must consciously delete to
# break the build.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.c         text eol=lf
*.h         text eol=lf
*.S         text eol=lf
*.ld        text eol=lf
*.mk        text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
Kbuild      text eol=lf
Kconfig     text eol=lf
*.rs        text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.patch     text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.jsonc     text eol=lf
*.exempt    text eol=lf

# ── Binary ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never normalised, never diffed as text. Build output and images are gitignored
# (.gitignore) and never committed; these rules exist so that a stray one, or a
# diagram committed under project-management/, cannot be corrupted by the
# `text=auto` guess.
*.o      binary
*.a      binary
*.so     binary
*.ko     binary
*.elf    binary
*.bin    binary
*.img    binary
*.iso    binary
*.qcow2  binary
*.cpio   binary
*.gz     binary
*.xz     binary
*.zst    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
